#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each character is converted to its 8-bit ASCII representation, the "
"resulting bit stream is mapped to ``{+1, -1}`` (bit ``1`` → ``+1``, bit "
"``0`` → ``-1``) and every bit is held for *bit_period* samples (non-"
"return-to-zero). The encoded block is tiled to fill exactly ``N`` "
"samples, mirroring :func:`binary_message`."
msgstr ""
"Each character is converted to its 8-bit ASCII representation, the "
"resulting bit stream is mapped to ``{+1, -1}`` (bit ``1`` → ``+1``, bit "
"``0`` → ``-1``) and every bit is held for *bit_period* samples (non-"
"return-to-zero). The encoded block is tiled to fill exactly ``N`` "
"samples, mirroring :func:`binary_message`."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:9 of
msgid ""
"Unlike :func:`binary_message` (a periodic square wave), this produces an "
"irregular run-length pattern that resembles a real digital transmission, "
"which is what the ``comm-*`` figures use as their information-bearing "
"message."
msgstr ""
"Unlike :func:`binary_message` (a periodic square wave), this produces an "
"irregular run-length pattern that resembles a real digital transmission, "
"which is what the ``comm-*`` figures use as their information-bearing "
"message."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:14 of
msgid ""
"Message text. Must contain only ASCII characters so it can be encoded to "
"a single byte per character."
msgstr ""
"Message text. Must contain only ASCII characters so it can be encoded to "
"a single byte per character."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:17 of
msgid "Number of samples each bit is held. Must be a positive integer."
msgstr "Number of samples each bit is held. Must be a positive integer."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:19 of
msgid "The BPSK message samples, each ``+1.0`` or ``-1.0``."
msgstr "The BPSK message samples, each ``+1.0`` or ``-1.0``."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:22 of
msgid "If ``bit_period`` is not a positive integer or ``text`` is empty."
msgstr "If ``bit_period`` is not a positive integer or ``text`` is empty."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:23 of
msgid "If ``text`` contains characters outside the ASCII range."
msgstr "If ``text`` contains characters outside the ASCII range."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.text_message:27 of
msgid "``\"A\"`` encodes to ``0b01000001``; with one sample per bit this is"
msgstr "``\"A\"`` encodes to ``0b01000001``; with one sample per bit this is"



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.sinusoidal_message:3 of
msgid ""
"Useful for frequency-response characterisation: feeding the output of "
"this function through the transmitter/channel/receiver chain shows the "
"system's gain and phase at one specific frequency."
msgstr ""
"Useful for frequency-response characterisation: feeding the output of "
"this function through the transmitter/channel/receiver chain shows the "
"system's gain and phase at one specific frequency."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.sinusoidal_message:7 of
msgid "Number of samples to produce."
msgstr "Number of samples to produce."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.sinusoidal_message:8 of
msgid ""
"Frequency in cycles per sample. Must satisfy ``0 < f < 0.5`` to avoid "
"aliasing (Nyquist at ``f = 0.5``). The default of ``0.1`` gives ten "
"samples per cycle."
msgstr ""
"Frequency in cycles per sample. Must satisfy ``0 < f < 0.5`` to avoid "
"aliasing (Nyquist at ``f = 0.5``). The default of ``0.1`` gives ten "
"samples per cycle."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.sinusoidal_message:12 of
msgid "The samples ``sin(2π · normalised_freq · n)`` for ``n = 0, 1, …, N − 1``."
msgstr "The samples ``sin(2π · normalised_freq · n)`` for ``n = 0, 1, …, N − 1``."



#: chaotic_pfc.dynamics.signals.sinusoidal_message:16 of
msgid "If *normalised_freq* is not strictly between 0 and 0.5."
msgstr "If *normalised_freq* is not strictly between 0 and 0.5."



